// Fibonacci numbers, as many as fit in one byte (up to 233).
// Numbers wrap past 255, so the loop runs while the sequence is still
// increasing: after 233 the next value wraps around to 121 and we stop.
// Shows variables, a loop, and the text cursor (print, newline).
a = 0
b = 1
count = 0
while b >= a {
    print(b)
    count = count + 1
    if count == 3 {          // three numbers per row (the screen is 64 pixels wide)
        newline()
        count = 0
    }
    next = a + b
    a = b
    b = next
}
